Upstream's package-lock.json for this release is missing the "resolved"
(tarball URL) and "integrity" fields for the vast majority of its entries --
a known class of npm lockfile bug (see
https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/6301). Without these fields,
prefetch-npm-deps has no way to know where to fetch a given package from, or
how to verify it, so it silently skips caching it. This later causes
`npm ci` to fail during the offline build phase with e.g. `ENOTCACHED` for
whichever package npm happens to need first (e.g. zone.js).

This patch fills in the missing "resolved" and "integrity" fields with the
real data queried from the npm registry for each affected package/version,
so the values are exactly what upstream's own registry serves.

